                {
                    "question": "Is there a vegetarian or vegan substitute for bonito flakes?",
                    "answer": "Dried shiitake mushrooms and kombu together make the closest vegetarian dashi; commercial vegan dashi powders made from kombu and shiitake also exist and work as a direct swap for instant dashi granules.",
                },
                {
                    "question": "Why do bonito flakes move on top of hot food?",
                    "answer": "The flakes are shaved so thin that rising heat and steam physically lift and curl them; it's a purely mechanical effect from their thinness, not a sign of freshness.",
                },
                {
                    "question": "Can bonito flakes be reused after making dashi?",
                    "answer": "Yes, for a second, weaker batch called niban dashi, often simmered longer with the spent flakes and kombu to pull out remaining flavor for miso soup or simmered dishes.",
                },
