                "Pour the vodka or eau de vie over the crushed currants so they're fully submerged. Seal the jar tightly.",
                "Store the jar in a cool, dark place for 6 to 8 weeks, gently swirling it every few days to redistribute the fruit. This steeping time is passive and isn't counted in the active prep or cook time above.",
                "Strain the infused liquid through a fine-mesh sieve lined with cheesecloth into a bowl, pressing the solids gently to extract liquid without forcing pulp through. Discard the spent currants.",
                "Combine the sugar and water in a small saucepan over medium heat, stirring until the sugar fully dissolves, about 3 to 4 minutes. Remove from heat and let the syrup cool completely to room temperature.",
