                "Arrange the ribs in a single layer in a 9x13-inch baking dish. Whisk the chicken broth and apple cider vinegar together and pour around (not over) the ribs.",
                "Cover the dish tightly with foil and braise for 2 to 2.5 hours, until the ribs are fork-tender and register at least 200°F (93°C) internally.",
