                "Preheat the oven to 250°F (120°C). Set the steak on a wire rack over a baking sheet so air circulates underneath.",
                "Roast until an instant-read thermometer reads about 10-15°F below your target finished temperature: pull at 110-115°F (43-46°C) for a final medium-rare of 130-135°F (54-57°C). This takes roughly 35-50 minutes depending on thickness.",
                "Rest the steak on the rack for 5-10 minutes while a heavy skillet, preferably cast iron, heats over high heat until it just starts to smoke.",
                "Add a high-smoke-point oil like avocado or refined vegetable oil, then sear the steak for 60-90 seconds per side, pressing down lightly for even contact. Add a tablespoon of butter, plus garlic and thyme if using, and baste the steak for the last 30 seconds.",
