                "Peeling from the bottom of the tail instead of the top: starting at the top segments makes the shell come away in fewer pieces.",
                "Pulling the tail meat out sideways instead of straight: it tears the meat and leaves half of it stuck in the shell.",
                "Avoiding the head because it looks unappetizing: the fat inside is what carries the boil's spice and butter flavor, not the shell meat alone.",
                "Over-squeezing the tail before peeling: too much pressure crushes the meat along with the shell.",
