                "Working in small batches, dredge the squid in cornstarch, shaking off the excess, and fry for 60-90 seconds until just cooked through but pale. Remove to a wire rack; do not crowd the pot, or the oil temperature will drop and the coating will turn greasy instead of crisp.",
                "Raise the oil temperature to 375°F (190°C). Return the squid to the oil in batches and fry a second time for 45-60 seconds, until deep golden and audibly crisp when tapped with tongs. Drain on the rack again.",
                "Pour off all but 1 tablespoon of oil from a clean skillet, add the garlic and chile, and stir-fry over medium-high heat for 30 seconds until fragrant but not browned.",
