                "Cutting an unripe fruit: the flesh should give slightly under gentle pressure, like a ripe kiwi; a rock-hard dragon fruit will taste bland and starchy.",
                "Scooping too close to the skin: a thin layer of flesh right under the peel is more fibrous and less sweet, so stop the spoon about a quarter inch short of the skin if texture matters.",
