                "Bring the lemon to room temperature, or microwave it for 15-20 seconds if it's cold from the fridge, this loosens the membranes inside.",
                "Roll the lemon firmly on the counter under your palm for about 10 seconds, pressing down as you go, to break down the internal pulp.",
                "Slice the lemon in half crosswise (through the equator, not through the stem end) to expose the most segments to the reamer.",
                "Press and twist a citrus reamer or handheld juicer into each half over a bowl, squeezing from the outside in to force juice out of the pulp pockets.",
                "Pour the juice through a fine-mesh strainer set over a measuring cup to catch seeds and pulp while keeping the juice.",
                "Check the measuring cup against the recipe amount; one medium lemon rarely covers more than 3 tablespoons, so juice extra lemons if a recipe needs 1/4 cup or more.",
