                "Shred a block of sharp cheddar rather than using bagged pre-shredded cheese; pre-shredded cheese is coated in anti-caking starches that make sauces grainy and thin instead of smooth.",
                "For a meltier sauce without losing the sharp bite, swap one of the four cups of cheddar for Monterey Jack or Gruyere, both melt more smoothly than aged cheddar on its own.",
                "Extra-sharp cheddar gives a stronger tang; if using it, cut the mustard powder to 1/2 teaspoon so the flavor doesn't turn bitter.",
                "White sharp cheddar works identically to orange sharp cheddar, the color comes from annatto and doesn't affect melt or flavor.",
