                {
                    "question": "Why is the consomme orange-red instead of brown?",
                    "answer": "The color comes from dried guajillo and ancho chiles blended into the braising liquid along with tomato; the fat that rises to the surface picks up that pigment, which is what tints the tortillas when they're dipped before frying.",
                },
                {
                    "question": "Can quesabirria be made with chicken?",
                    "answer": "Yes, though it's a nontraditional shortcut. Bone-in chicken thighs braise in about half the time of beef or goat, but the resulting consomme is thinner and less rich since chicken renders far less fat.",
                },
                {
                    "question": "How do you reheat quesabirria tacos without them going soft?",
                    "answer": "Reheat them in a dry skillet or on a griddle over medium heat for a few minutes per side rather than in a microwave, which softens the crisp shell. Warm the consomme separately in a small saucepan.",
                },
