                {
                    "question": "Why does malt vinegar taste different from white vinegar?",
                    "answer": "Malt vinegar starts as an ale-like fermented barley liquid before it's converted to acetic acid, which carries over malty, slightly sweet, bread-like notes that distilled white vinegar, made from pure grain alcohol, doesn't have.",
                },
