                "In the same pot, add the onion and cook for 3 minutes, until softened. Add the tomatoes and garlic and cook another 3 minutes, until the tomatoes break down slightly.",
                "Transfer the onion, tomato, and garlic mixture to a blender with 1 cup of the beef broth. Blend until smooth.",
                "Return the browned beef to the pot along with the blended sauce, remaining beef broth, cumin, oregano, and bay leaves. Bring to a simmer, then cover, reduce heat to low, and cook for 1.5 hours, until the beef is fork-tender.",
