                "Serve the finished peas over cooked white rice to turn this into Hoppin' John, another Southern New Year's tradition believed to bring luck and prosperity.",
                "Canned black-eyed peas work in a pinch: skip the soaking step, sauté the vegetables and bacon as directed, then add 4 drained 15-ounce cans of peas with just 2 cups of broth and simmer 20 minutes to let the flavors combine.",
