                "Submerge the turkey legs fully in the brine, weighing them down with a plate if needed. Cover and refrigerate for 8-12 hours.",
                "Remove the legs from the brine, rinse briefly, and pat completely dry with paper towels. Set them on a wire rack over a baking sheet, uncovered, and refrigerate for at least 1 hour (or up to overnight) to dry out the skin.",
