                "For the caramel sauce: spread the granulated sugar in an even layer in a separate dry, light-colored skillet over medium heat. Let it melt undisturbed for 2-3 minutes until the edges turn amber, then gently swirl the pan (don't stir with a utensil) until fully melted and deep amber, about 3 more minutes.",
                "Remove from heat and carefully whisk in the remaining 2 tablespoons butter, then slowly stream in 1/4 cup of the cream (it will bubble hard). Whisk in the vanilla and 1/4 teaspoon salt until smooth.",
