                "After roasting the turkey or chicken, pour the pan drippings into a heatproof measuring cup and let the fat rise to the top for a few minutes.",
                "Skim 4 tablespoons of the fat back into the roasting pan or a saucepan set over medium heat (use butter if there isn't enough fat). Whisk in the flour and cook, stirring constantly, for 2-3 minutes until the roux turns a light golden brown and smells toasty.",
