                "Place the cut fries in a large bowl of cold water with the vinegar and soak for at least 30 minutes, up to overnight in the fridge. This pulls out surface starch that would otherwise make the fries gummy.",
                "Drain the fries and spread them on a clean kitchen towel, patting them completely dry. Any surface water will make the tallow spit and lower the oil temperature.",
