                "Rub a thin, even layer of mustard over both sides of each rack, then pack the dry rub on generously, pressing it into the meat. Let the ribs sit at room temperature for 30 minutes, or refrigerate uncovered for up to 8 hours for a firmer bark.",
                "Preheat the oven to 275°F (135°C). Set a wire rack inside a foil-lined rimmed baking sheet and arrange the ribs bone-side down.",
